{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1189324-yanking-trinity-psychics-for-the-world-of-darkness","id":1189324,"title":"Yanking Trinity Psychics for the World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-24T18:05:52-08:00","id":1189324,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Yanking Trinity Psychics for the World of Darkness","content":"So Sorcerer Revised has a suggestion on importing Psychics into in the World of Darkness for more potent Psychic options. So I am really considering this now due to the Renaissance of the new Aeon book. I'm still pretty new to Trinity, but looking at the previews it looks like Psi could be comparable to major splats. So what about importing them as say a consequence of the Red Star. Perhaps Quantum is a mysterious Force flooding into the world at the end of days invoking an Evolutionary leap. So instead of Aberrants appearing in the World of Darkness a small number of high level psychics are appearing..<br /> <br /> What are thoughts and ideas on this? Any input from those who know the system better? What about merging Trinity Ideas with the supernatural concepts of the World of Darkness for things like Spirit based Psi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T21:07:42-08:00","id":1189339,"title":"","content":"First off, a nitpick: Quantum and Sub-Quantum (i.e., Psi) are separate, conflicting things. The first is responsible for Aberrants, the second is responsible for Psions and Psiads. Which leads me to my second point: <br /> <br /> Psiads are \u201cnaturally occurring\u201d psychics; they tend to have less power than Psions but more versatility. Psions are psychics whose powers have been triggered by a mysterious piece of hypertech called a Prometheus Chamber. In the process, the chamber strengthens their powers but also narrows their scope. If you're going with the notion of psychics spontaneously appearing after the Red Star, you may want to consider going with Psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}